From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: R5900: sqrt.s reads its operand from ft

On the R5900 the FPU takes the operand of SQRT.S from the ft field of
the instruction, where every other MIPS uses fs (the EE Core
Instruction Set Manual writes it "SQRT.S fd, ft"). The table had only
the standard form, so "sqrt.s $f0, $f12" was encoded with $f12 in fs,
and the hardware took the square root of $f0 instead. GCC emits
sqrt.s for sqrtf() with -march=r5900, so every program with a square
root in float got a wrong number.

Add the R5900 form, with the standard one no longer for the R5900, so
the disassembler shows the right register as well.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port; a candidate for upstream]
---
--- a/opcodes/mips-opc.c	2026-10-17 12:09:50.228649571 +0100
+++ b/opcodes/mips-opc.c	2026-10-17 12:09:50.242320262 +0100
@@ -1945,7 +1945,9 @@
 {"sqc2",		"+7,o(b)",	0xf8000000, 0xfc000000,	RD_3|RD_C2|SM,		0,		EE,		0,	0 },
 {"sqc2",		"+7,A(b)",	0,    (int) M_SQC2_AB,	INSN_MACRO,		0,		EE,		0,	0 },
 {"sqrt.d",		"D,S",		0x46200004, 0xffff003f, WR_1|RD_2|FP_D,		0,		I2,		0,	SF },
-{"sqrt.s",		"D,S",		0x46000004, 0xffff003f, WR_1|RD_2|FP_S,		0,		I2,		0,	0 },
+/* The R5900 reads the operand of sqrt.s from the ft field, not fs.  */
+{"sqrt.s",		"D,T",		0x46000004, 0xffe0f83f, WR_1|RD_2|FP_S,		0,		EE,		0,	0 },
+{"sqrt.s",		"D,S",		0x46000004, 0xffff003f, WR_1|RD_2|FP_S,		0,		I2,		0,	EE },
 {"sqrt.ps",		"D,S",		0x46c00004, 0xffff003f, WR_1|RD_2|FP_D,		0,		SB1,		0,	0 },
 {"srav",		"d,t,s",	0x00000007, 0xfc0007ff,	WR_1|RD_2|RD_3,		0,		I1,		0,	0 },
 {"sra",			"d,w,s",	0x00000007, 0xfc0007ff,	WR_1|RD_2|RD_3,		0,		I1,		0,	0 }, /* srav */
